{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLgrTRn1WWk5DqQq4caQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the bug with a one-line change in `astropy/modeling/separable.py:245`, inside `_cstack`, which builds the matrix for the `&` operator.\n\n**Cause:** When the right-hand side of `&` was already a nested compound model, its separability had been worked out as a matrix. But `_cstack` filled that whole block with `1` instead of copying the matrix in, so every input and output in it looked linked to every other one:\n```python\ncright[-right.shape[0]:, -right.shape[1]:] = 1      # before\ncright[-right.shape[0]:, -right.shape[1]:] = right  # after\n```\nThe left-hand side already did this correctly (`cleft[...] = left`). Only the right side had the bug.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `separability_matrix(m.Pix2Sky_TAN() & (m.Linear1D(10) & m.Linear1D(5)))` now gives the expected block-diagonal result, with the two linear models separable.\n- I couldn't run pytest here: one way it fails to load an astropy test plugin, the other way it clashes with the astropy copy installed in the environment. Instead I called the 11 test functions and parametrized cases in `astropy/modeling/tests/test_separable.py` directly from Python, and all passed. Pytest-only setup like fixtures or conftest wasn't exercised that way.\n\nI didn't add a regression test for the nested case, since the rules say not to touch test files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":253,"cache_read_input_tokens":21728,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":253},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35b842bc-274a-4d25-a1c4-97252795e686","uuid":"8822f546-698b-46b1-9b5c-1abd0a0040a1","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:58:20.678Z","request_id":"req_011ChLgrTHqg2s42JVxykrHk"}
